Network use (AGPL-3.0 section 13)
---------------------------------
If you run a modified version of OpenCorpoChat and let users interact with it
over a network, you must offer those users the Corresponding Source of your
modified version. The application includes a "Source code" link in its About
dialog for this purpose; point it at your fork by setting OCPC_SOURCE_URL.

Third-party software
--------------------
OpenCorpoChat depends on third-party open-source packages, each under its own
license. A complete list with license texts is generated for every release in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (run `pnpm licenses:check --write` to produce it
locally). All dependencies are checked in CI against an AGPL-3.0-compatible
license allowlist.

Icons are from Lucide (https://lucide.dev), ISC License.
Emoji are rendered using the viewer's platform Unicode emoji font; no emoji
image assets are distributed with this project.

